obi-wan kenobi's whole existence in the  star wars universe is tied up with the  fate of anakin skywalker and their  history is even longer and more  complicated than you might think this is  obi-wan's history with darth vader  explained  in the phantom menace obi-wan tells his  master qui-gon jinn that he senses  they've picked up another pathetic life  form referring to the young anakin  skywalker  this line demonstrates how from the very  beginning obi-wan didn't think they  needed extra baggage on their quest to  stop the trade federation's invasion of  naboo in fact obi-wan and anakin never  seem to gel in the phantom menace  as qui-gon waits to hear if the jedi  council will accept anakin as an  apprentice obi-wan even points out that  his master's defiance is preventing his  promotion to the council itself obi-wan  strictly adheres to the jedi code and  takes issue with qui-gon's constant  rebellion against it however when  qui-gon is killed by darth maul his  dying request is that obi-wan trained  the young anakin obi-wan himself briefly  takes on qui-gon's rebellious spirit  when he tells yoda he will train anakin  to fulfill this wish regardless of  whether the council approves obi-wan's  general fidelity to the jedi order and  its rules frequently contrasts with the  older anakin's perpetual rebellion  against them however the decision to go  against the council in the first place  is handed down by qui-gon who planted a  seed for the rift that would one day  tear the galaxy apart  from the start anakin skywalker is  depicted as a man of action while  obi-wan is a more careful and analytical  fighter a perfect example of this takes  place in attack of the clones when  anakin rushes in to fight count dooku  only to be knocked out by his enemies  force lightning meanwhile obi-wan  chooses to take a more defensive  approach and lasts longer in battle  because of it while anakin is seen as  something of a prodigy his reckless  actions often lead obi-wan to regard his  apprentice with exasperation as well as  admiration in the clone wars series  obi-wan frequently scolds anakin for  being too foolhardy while anakin often  calls out obi-wan for being too hesitant  we don't need the whole fleet i can do  this myself anakin slow down and do what  i tell you  it's more important to save lives than  destroy ships  anakin leaps into battle without  thinking about it and thanks to his  abilities always makes it out on the  other side on the other hand obi-wan  always tries to evaluate every situation  in order to come up with a proper plan  of course it's anakin's reckless need to  take action that eventually leads him to  the dark side no doubt the older obi-wan  would have wished that he had taken this  character flaw of anakin's far more  seriously  a key facet of the jedi code is that  force users should always avoid personal  attachments  anakin shows us why this principle is so  important because his love of padme  allows palpatine to manipulate him into  joining the dark side however anakin's  attachment to his relationships isn't  exclusive to padme it also includes  obi-wan himself obi-wan is a great  mentor  as wise as master yoda and  as powerful as master windu  attack of the clones demonstrates how  deep their relationship goes when anakin  sees obi-wan come under attack by  droidikas anakin had earlier pointed out  that obi-wan is the closest thing he has  to a father and he clearly wants to save  him from the droids but he's torn  between that desire and his duty to  protect padme thankfully padme actually  suggests trying to save obi-wan  themselves giving anakin the opportunity  to set out to rescue his master of  course it is this shared mission that  cements anakin and padme's love after  their rescue mission fails and the two  are sentenced to execution in a  gladiatorial arena they share a kiss  that later leads to marriage anakin's  inability to deny his personal  relationships is a flaw in his jedi  mindset that recurs throughout the  prequel era eventually leading to his  fall from grace  his affection for obi-wan is a central  issue in this dynamic making the history  that anakin padme and obi-wan share a  very dangerous thing  the phantom menace ends with obi-wan as  a full jedi knight and anakin as a  padawan a decade later attack of the  clones ends with anakin's marriage and  the beginning of the clone wars  following that the clone wars covers the  three-year gap between attack of the  clones and revenge of the sith given the  amount of ground the series covers it  has to be inferred that when the first  battle of geonosis takes place and the  war begins anakin is immediately  promoted to jedi knight as both he and  obi-wan are generals in the clone wars  from that time on obi-wan and anakin are  seen as colleagues on more or less the  same level and they are generally given  the same level of responsibility in most  situations  it's worth remembering however that not  only had anakin just been promoted but  he started his training considerably  later in life than most jedi if anakin  had bristled that obi-wan's instruction  before no doubt he really resents any  perceived seniority by this point  obi-wan however never seems to begrudge  the fact that anakin skips ahead to  become his equal  anakin skywalker was supposed to be  obi-wan student and you would expect a  master and student relationship to  continue in some shape or form even  after their formal training ends that  certainly seems to be the case with yoda  and his students as even count dooku  views his old master with respect  yet perhaps because of obi-wan and  anakin's closeness in age their equal  military ranks and anakin's exceptional  strength with the force they become more  like brothers than a student and a  teacher by the time anakin is a  full-fledged jedi he already seems to  think of himself as superior to his  master obi-wan is constantly advising  prudence while anakin almost always  thinks immediate action is the key to  victory this difference leads to  competition between the two as they seek  to prove that their approach is better  anakin is especially eager to prove that  he's stronger than obi-wan culminating  in their duel on mustafar in which  obi-wan insists anakin can't defeat him  the younger jedi acts rashly and is left  for dead as a result putting a final end  to their long and fateful sibling  rivalry  anakin tends to think that obi-wan is a  model of self-control to the point where  he mistakes obi-wan's adherence to the  austere jedi lifestyle for a lack of  emotion or passion yet we see in the  clone wars that obi-wan understands  anakin's longings more than skywalker  seem to realize he simply doesn't give  in to them take for instance obi-wan's  history with satin crees the ruler of  mandalore their relationship parallels  the dynamic between anakin and padme as  sateen is also a strong woman and a  political leader one clone war story arc  reveals that she and obi-wan once had a  romantic connection though it's never  clear if they acted on those feelings  however it's obvious obi-wan cares for  her and perhaps if he and anakin had  discussed their forbidden romances it  would have helped steer anakin away from  his eventual downfall despite what  anakin might think obi-wan also  questions the jedi order from time to  time this is first seen when he tells  yoda he will train anakin no matter what  the council decides but it is also made  apparent with his reaction to the jedi  order's vilification of ahsoka tano for  a crime he knows she did not commit  the real difference between those two  jedi is how they handle their issues  with the jedi order for all his power  anakin never learns to control his  emotions the way obi-wan does despite  obi-wan's pleas for his former padawan  to do so  in attack of the clones anakin angrily  complains to padme that obi-wan is  jealous and holding him back of course  this isn't the case at all obi-wan only  ever wants the best for anakin believing  that despite the boy's exceptional  skills with the force his padawan needed  to mature emotionally in order to become  a full jedi knight obviously obi-wan was  right several times in the clone wars  obi-wan tells anakin to play a situation  carefully only to watch as anakin rashly  springs into action sometimes it works  out but other times his brash choices  lead to high casualties or to obi-wan  having to rescue the young jedi  what anakin sees as obi-wan's jealousy  is actually his master's desire to guide  him to reach his full potential  eventually when obi-wan confronts darth  vader the former apprentice tells  obi-wan not to lecture him insisting  that he sees through the lies of the  jedi by extension he claims to see  through the supposed lies that obi-wan  had told him to keep him from fulfilling  his destiny  it's a tragic misinterpretation of their  entire relationship  in a new hope obi-wan says this of  anakin skywalker  he was the best star pilot in the galaxy  and a cunning warrior  more importantly though he adds  and he was a good friend  anakin's inability to identify and  control his emotions was a weakness that  palpatine easily exploited on the other  hand obi-wan may have felt a more  profound love for anakin than his  apprentice felt for him simply remaining  in control of those feelings obi-wan's  heart breaks when he watches the  security footage of anakin killing  younglings and on mustafar obi-wan  laments that he has failed his young  apprentice  obi-wan retreated to the life of a  hermit in order to hide from the empire  after the destruction of the jedi order  but you can't help but wonder whether he  also exiled himself as punishment for  preventing anakin from falling to the  dark side  when obi-wan appears in rebels a deep  sadness lingers over his bittersweet  victory against his longtime rival maul  in a new hope darth vader says that he  feels obi-wan's presence on the death  star so there can be no doubt that  obi-wan knew vader was there as well he  chooses to go alone on his mission in  part because the ever contemplative  obi-wan knows he will have to confront  his former apprentice  looking at their final showdown from  this point of view it is a reasonable  conclusion that obi-wan believes his  sacrifice to be a penance for failing  his old friend  after anakin becomes darth vader obi-wan  volunteers to watch over luke on  tatooine he didn't have to do this  however obi-wan could have left luke to  be raised by the lars family alone of  course he takes this mission in part out  of a desire to see a jedi re-emerge and  save the galaxy however another part of  him probably wants to protect the son of  a friend he once cared very deeply for  when obi-wan tells luke about his father  in a new hope he hides the true nature  of his relationship to darth vader  telling luke that vader betrayed and  murdered anakin skywalker  in return of the jedi obi-wan famously  claims that anakin ceased to exist once  he became vader and that what he told  luke was true from a certain point of  view it stands to reason that obi-wan  would have held on to his feelings for  his lost brother and that he probably  saw it as his duty to watch over and  protect his son  it's a well-known fact that obi-wan won  his victory over anakin on mustafar  because of his ability to claim the high  ground  this slight difference in elevation  allows obi-wan to slice off anakin's  limbs after he attempts to go for the  kill however this line applies to more  than just the physical difference  between the two jedi obi-wan has also  gained the moral high ground here and  it's hard to argue otherwise especially  considering that anakin has just  destroyed the jedi order he was sworn to  protect slaughtered the younglings and  attacked his own wife throughout the  prequels and the series obi-wan has a  firmer grasp of morality and duty than  anakin who often acts for selfish  reasons and while more stories in the  star wars galaxy may find obi-wan  struggling with the moral ambiguities of  life outside the order he will no doubt  always keep the high ground over his  former apprentice  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]  you

